        "id": 18914
      },
      "writtenOn": "2022-10-25T14:33:38Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Well I have them as separate blocks - both \u0027regular\u0027 blenders and primitive blenders both boil down to `SkBlenderBase`, right?\n\nOriginally, I had added an overloaded `SkBlenderBase::addToKey` that took in a color, and this is what distinguished a primitive blender. But we figured out that we don\u0027t know the color at this point in time and it cannot be stored as a uniform, so we no longer need to take in a color here. That\u0027s what motivated me to return to using this bool.\n\nInstead of keeping it as-is, what did you have in mind?\n1) A whole separate blender base class, like \u0027SkPrimitiveBlenderBase`, which has a .cpp file equivalent to `SkBlendModeBlender`; such as `SkPrimitiveBlender\u0027\n2) Adding a separate method to `SkBlenderBase` explicitly for primitive blenders that would be equivalent to \u0027addToKey\u0027; such as `SkBlenderBase::addPrimitiveBlenderToKey`\n3) Other?",
      "parentUuid": "38ae10d8_219fc4d5",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 71,
        "startChar": 29,
        "endLine": 71,
        "endChar": 55
      },
      "revId": "8319057f813f4a5d0dfbb0357cce5d0cc8b55709",
